From: komorebi <markovs.i.mail@gmail.com>
Subject: [PATCH] clutter/sprite: Hold the implicit grab on the actor its chain is for

A press outside the active seat grab gets an event chain made of the grab
actor alone (clutter_actor_collect_event_actors() treats the grab root as
extending infinitely), yet the implicit grab was recorded on the actor under
the pointer, which is not in that chain. Unmap tracking follows the recorded
actor, so when the grab actor went away while the sequence lasted - the
input-only actor of a Wayland popup or drag grab, destroyed when the client
dismisses it while a button is held - nothing pruned it, and the chain kept a
receiver that was no longer on the stage. A grab on the stage before the
release then cancelled every receiver in the "same grab actor" branch of
clutter_sprite_notify_grab() and hit its assertion.

Record the implicit grab on the grab actor in that case, so it is followed
like any other implicitly grabbed actor. For the same reason, take
target-phase actions from the grab actor rather than from the actor under
the pointer: that one is behind the grab and should not see the press.
---
 clutter/clutter/clutter-sprite.c | 17 +++++++++++++++--
 1 file changed, 15 insertions(+), 2 deletions(-)
--- a/clutter/clutter/clutter-sprite.c
+++ b/clutter/clutter/clutter-sprite.c
@@ -372,12 +372,18 @@
                              ClutterActor  *deepmost)
 {
   ClutterSpritePrivate *priv = clutter_sprite_get_instance_private (sprite);
+  ClutterActor *target;
   const GList *l;
   int i;
 
   g_assert (priv->cur_event_actors->len == 0);
   clutter_actor_collect_event_actors (topmost, deepmost, priv->cur_event_actors);
 
+  /* Outside topmost, the event goes to topmost alone (see
+   * clutter_actor_collect_event_actors()), which is then its target.
+   */
+  target = clutter_actor_contains (topmost, deepmost) ? deepmost : topmost;
+
   for (i = priv->cur_event_actors->len - 1; i >= 0; i--)
     {
       ClutterActor *actor = g_ptr_array_index (priv->cur_event_actors, i);
@@ -394,7 +400,7 @@
       add_actor_to_event_emission_chain (chain, actor, CLUTTER_PHASE_CAPTURE);
     }
 
-  for (l = clutter_actor_peek_actions (deepmost); l; l = l->next)
+  for (l = clutter_actor_peek_actions (target); l; l = l->next)
     {
       ClutterAction *action = l->data;
 
@@ -889,7 +895,14 @@
   if (is_sequence_begin && setup_implicit_grab (sprite))
     {
       g_assert (priv->implicit_grab_actor == NULL);
-      priv->implicit_grab_actor = target_actor;
+      /* The implicit grab is held by the actor its event chain is built for:
+       * outside the seat grab that is the grab actor, not the actor under the
+       * pointer, and it is the one to follow if it goes away while the
+       * sequence lasts.
+       */
+      priv->implicit_grab_actor =
+        clutter_actor_contains (seat_grab_actor, target_actor) ?
+        target_actor : seat_grab_actor;
       clutter_actor_set_implicitly_grabbed (priv->implicit_grab_actor, TRUE);
 
       create_event_emission_chain (sprite, priv->event_emission_chain, seat_grab_actor, target_actor);
